\section{Conclusions}
\vspace{-0.5em}
In this paper, we proposed a new framework for personalizing a universal RNNLM
using data crawled over social networks. 
The proposed approach is based on a user characteristic feature extracted
from the user corpus and friends corpora, which is not only user-dependent but sentence-dependent feature.
This universal RNNLM can predict different word distributions for different
users given the same context.
Experiments demonstrated really good improvements in both perplexity
and WER, and the proposed approach is much more robust to data
sparseness than the previous work.

